### Step 3 – Counting argument

> “If we have exactly \(k\) sunny lines, (2.5) yields \(k\bigl\lfloor\frac{k+1}{2}\bigr\rfloor\ge\frac{k(k+1)}2\).”

**Analysis:**  
Given the bound \(|\text{sunny line}\cap T_k|\le\lfloor (k+1)/2\rfloor\), the inequality follows directly. The subsequent parity analysis (even \(k\) impossible, odd \(k\) forces equality) is algebraically correct.

