**Analysis:**  
- For \(|p+q|=2\) we must have \(p+q=2\) or \(p+q=-2\).  
  - \(p=q=1\) indeed satisfies \(p+q=2\).  
  - \(p=-2,\;q=1\) gives \(p+q=-1\), **not** \(|p+q|=2\).  
