The lines listed above **do not** pass through these points for any \(n>3\). For example, when \(n=4\) the uncovered points are \((2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,1),(3,2),(4,1)\); none of the three given lines contains \((2,3)\) or \((4,1)\). Hence the construction fails for all \(n\ge4\). A correct construction would require the three lines to be shifted horizontally (e.g. \(y=x-n+3,\; y=-2x+2n-1,\; y=-\tfrac12x+\tfrac n2+1\)), but such a shift is never mentioned.

